# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PRIVATE SOURCE DATA — this repository is PUBLIC (GitHub Pages serves from it).
#
# data/ holds the raw genealogical source: full names, exact dates of birth and
# birth places for people who are alive, including minors, plus curation notes
# about a disputed paternity. None of it may ever enter a public commit.
#
# What ships instead is docs/data/tree.json, produced by tools/build_site.py,
# which redacts every living person down to a surname. If you need the
# unredacted build, run the generator with --include-living and DO NOT commit
# the result — it is covered by the docs/data/tree.private.json rule below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leading slash matters: an unanchored "data/" would also match docs/data/,
# which is the generated public payload that has to ship.
/data/
docs/data/tree.private.json
*.ged

# Family photographs, dropped into the repo root but NOT published. Publishing
# images is a separate decision from publishing the tree, and it has not been
# made. Note that a path can leak as surely as a file: one of these folders is
# named after a living person, so even the directory listing would have to be
# reworked before any of this could ship.
/Family photos/
/media/
